<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="031" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-12 — publish-size re-baseline on net10 + governance-doc updates</title>
    <phase>P3 Test green + re-baseline</phase>
    <gate>030 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Writes to root CLAUDE.md §10 + .claude/ constraint (main-session-only); binding publish-size governance number.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Measure + record + update two governance docs; well-specified.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Writes root CLAUDE.md + .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md — MAIN-SESSION-ONLY per root §3 sub-agent write boundary.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030</deps>
    <tags>dotnet, bff-api, deployment, governance, skill-directives, root-claude-md</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Measure the net10 compressed `dotnet publish -c Release` output for the BFF and re-baseline the §10 publish-size governance number. Report the absolute compressed size + the diff vs the ~49.63 MB (incl-PDB) baseline, confirm it is ≤60 MB, and update the number in root `CLAUDE.md` §10 AND `.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md`. State the PDB-inclusion convention when reporting. This is a MAIN-SESSION-ONLY write task (touches root CLAUDE.md + `.claude/`).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in framework-dependent publish sizing, zip-entry accounting, and Spaarke's BFF publish-hygiene governance. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The net10 compressed publish size is measured and recorded (absolute + diff vs 49.63 MB incl-PDB); ≤60 MB confirmed; root `CLAUDE.md` §10 and `.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md` both carry the new baseline number with the PDB convention stated; measurement captured in `notes/publish-size-rebaseline.md`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec FR-12 + NFR-02 + design §10. Baseline 2026-07-08 = ~49.63 MB incl PDBs / 45.87 MB excl. A framework-version bump WILL shift the baseline. FR-04 pin removals + FR-06 classic-SDK removal REDUCE surface, so the net delta may be small or negative. ADR-029 forbids self-contained. The publish-size rule (`.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md` "BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule") + root CLAUDE.md §10 both encode the number — update BOTH.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/publish-size-rebaseline.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">Full suite green — the code being published is final.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Publish framework-dependent linux-x64 into `deploy/api-publish/`; measure COMPRESSED output; keep the wwwroot sourcemap exclusion. ≤60 MB ceiling (NFR-02).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MAIN-SESSION-ONLY: this task edits root `CLAUDE.md` + `.claude/constraints/` — a sub-agent CANNOT write those (root §3). Run it in the main session.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST state the PDB-inclusion convention when reporting; update BOTH governance locations to the same number.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>BFF publish-size re-baseline + governance</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="publish-size-rule" location=".claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md">"BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule (NFR-01)" — the exact measure-and-report procedure.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-12 + ADR-029 + the publish-size rule. Declare RIGOR: FULL. Confirm MAIN SESSION (not a sub-agent) for the `.claude/`/root writes.</step>
    <step order="1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; produce the compressed zip; measure size + entry count.</step>
    <step order="2">Record absolute compressed size + diff vs 49.63 MB (incl-PDB), stating the PDB convention, in `notes/publish-size-rebaseline.md`.</step>
    <step order="3">Confirm ≤60 MB. If ≥+5 MB single-task delta or ≥55 MB cumulative, flag per the escalation ladder.</step>
    <step order="4">Update root `CLAUDE.md` §10 baseline number and `.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md` (both "Publish & Packaging" + the per-task rule) to the new number + date.</step>
    <step order="5">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 031 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the net10 compressed publish is ≥55 MB (cumulative architecture-review threshold) or ≥+5 MB vs baseline, STOP and surface per CLAUDE.md §10 escalation ladder before updating the governance number; ≥60 MB is a HARD STOP requiring an ADR-029 amendment.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Publish BFF</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">CLAUDE.md (§10 baseline number)</output>
    <output type="doc">.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md (baseline number)</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/publish-size-rebaseline.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The net10 compressed publish size is measured and ≤60 MB, reported as absolute + diff vs 49.63 MB with the PDB convention stated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Root `CLAUDE.md` §10 AND `.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md` both carry the new baseline number + date.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the publish is framework-dependent (no self-contained `runtimes/` tree); no `PublishTrimmed`/`PublishAot`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If ≥55 MB or ≥+5 MB, the escalation was surfaced before the doc update.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-12 + NFR-02. Main-session-only per root §3. The r3 handoff note (task 090) must record that this baseline moved.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
